{"authored" [{"question" "q-14313" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}}$  that satisfies $y(1)=2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037336/state.json" "file_sha256" "f453a8267dda6772768fb5cc64ac599b02883620473cd19645b4409abff5842a" "basis" 1262 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037336/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-14313" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find the particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}} \\\\ {y}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={x}^{2} \\\\ \\int {y}^{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{3}}{3} & =\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+{C}_{1} \\\\ {y}^{3} & ={x}^{3}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere   $C=3{C}_{1}$ is an arbitrary constant.  \n\nWe now apply the condition $y(1)=2$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{2}^{3} & ={1}^{3}+C \\\\ 8-1 & =C \\\\ C & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we get the particular solution in implicit form:\n\n$$\n{y}^{3}={x}^{3}+7.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037336/state.json" "file_sha256" "f453a8267dda6772768fb5cc64ac599b02883620473cd19645b4409abff5842a" "basis" 1262 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037336/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-14313" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037336/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e88c4fa705fe5f93bbdcbe23baa488aa4a8e76a12e3e691a6f6f1f28a24352e5" "basis" 1262 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037336/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-14313" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037336/state.json" "file_sha256" "f453a8267dda6772768fb5cc64ac599b02883620473cd19645b4409abff5842a" "basis" 1262 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037336/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-14313" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{y}^{3}=2{x}^{3}+2"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037336/state.json" "file_sha256" "f453a8267dda6772768fb5cc64ac599b02883620473cd19645b4409abff5842a" "basis" 1262 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037336/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-14313" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{y}^{3}=3{x}^{2}+5"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037336/state.json" "file_sha256" "f453a8267dda6772768fb5cc64ac599b02883620473cd19645b4409abff5842a" "basis" 1262 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037336/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-14313" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{y}^{3}=5{x}^{3}+3"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037336/state.json" "file_sha256" "f453a8267dda6772768fb5cc64ac599b02883620473cd19645b4409abff5842a" "basis" 1262 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037336/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-14313" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{y}^{3}={x}^{2}+3"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037336/state.json" "file_sha256" "f453a8267dda6772768fb5cc64ac599b02883620473cd19645b4409abff5842a" "basis" 1262 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037336/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-14313" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{y}^{3}={x}^{3}+7"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037336/state.json" "file_sha256" "f453a8267dda6772768fb5cc64ac599b02883620473cd19645b4409abff5842a" "basis" 1262 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037336/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-4016" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{x-2y}$ that satisfies $y(0)=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057251/state.json" "file_sha256" "d942c17668b6e101603addfb72b0704974093f70ed9d0e7dce49d04bf8550d8b" "basis" 1861 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057251/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-4016" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{x-2y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{x}\\cdot {e}^{-2y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{e}^{x}}{{e}^{2y}} \\\\ {e}^{2y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{x} \\\\ \\int {e}^{2y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {e}^{2y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int {e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2y} & ={e}^{x}+{C}_{1} \\\\ {e}^{2y} & =2{e}^{x}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=2{C}_{1}$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nApplying the natural logarithm to both sides, we find the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{2y}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2{e}^{x}+C) \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2{e}^{x}+C).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now apply the condition $y(0)=0$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2{e}^{0}+C) & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+C) & =0 \\\\ 2+C & =1 \\\\ C & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{x-2y}$ that satisfies the condition $y(0)=0$ is\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2{e}^{x}-1).\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057251/state.json" "file_sha256" "d942c17668b6e101603addfb72b0704974093f70ed9d0e7dce49d04bf8550d8b" "basis" 1861 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057251/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-4016" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057251/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d6cd6ea9028bcde8009f6010933e7dd4de81e8a086f50ec223aba3e414f32cc2" "basis" 1861 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057251/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-4016" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057251/state.json" "file_sha256" "d942c17668b6e101603addfb72b0704974093f70ed9d0e7dce49d04bf8550d8b" "basis" 1861 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057251/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-4016" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2{e}^{x}-1)"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057251/state.json" "file_sha256" "d942c17668b6e101603addfb72b0704974093f70ed9d0e7dce49d04bf8550d8b" "basis" 1861 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057251/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-4016" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057251/state.json" "file_sha256" "d942c17668b6e101603addfb72b0704974093f70ed9d0e7dce49d04bf8550d8b" "basis" 1861 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057251/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-4016" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4{e}^{x}-3)"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057251/state.json" "file_sha256" "d942c17668b6e101603addfb72b0704974093f70ed9d0e7dce49d04bf8550d8b" "basis" 1861 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057251/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-4016" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2-{e}^{x})"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057251/state.json" "file_sha256" "d942c17668b6e101603addfb72b0704974093f70ed9d0e7dce49d04bf8550d8b" "basis" 1861 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057251/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-4016" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{{e}^{x}+1}{2})"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057251/state.json" "file_sha256" "d942c17668b6e101603addfb72b0704974093f70ed9d0e7dce49d04bf8550d8b" "basis" 1861 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057251/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-4016" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2{e}^{x}-1)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057251/state.json" "file_sha256" "d942c17668b6e101603addfb72b0704974093f70ed9d0e7dce49d04bf8550d8b" "basis" 1861 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057251/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-4016" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{x-2y}$ that satisfies $y(0)=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067140/state.json" "file_sha256" "e8f91deb7026399670eb9b3617edc6d586239baad65addd848701991e2502eb4"} {"question" "q-4016" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{x-2y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{x}\\cdot {e}^{-2y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{e}^{x}}{{e}^{2y}} \\\\ {e}^{2y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{x} \\\\ \\int {e}^{2y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {e}^{2y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int {e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2y} & ={e}^{x}+{C}_{1} \\\\ {e}^{2y} & =2{e}^{x}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=2{C}_{1}$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nApplying the natural logarithm to both sides, we find the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{2y}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2{e}^{x}+C) \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2{e}^{x}+C).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now apply the condition $y(0)=0$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2{e}^{0}+C) & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+C) & =0 \\\\ 2+C & =1 \\\\ C & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{x-2y}$ that satisfies the condition $y(0)=0$ is\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2{e}^{x}-1).\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067140/state.json" "file_sha256" "e8f91deb7026399670eb9b3617edc6d586239baad65addd848701991e2502eb4"} {"question" "q-4016" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067140/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6c097b443fe834d701881765ef06b2ccca34858447fd15a076ba25dbfa4614f6"} {"question" "q-4016" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067140/state.json" "file_sha256" "e8f91deb7026399670eb9b3617edc6d586239baad65addd848701991e2502eb4"} {"question" "q-4016" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2{e}^{x}-1)"] ["math" "y=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)"] ["math" "y=\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4{e}^{x}-3)"] ["math" "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2-{e}^{x})"] ["math" "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{{e}^{x}+1}{2})"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067140/state.json" "file_sha256" "e8f91deb7026399670eb9b3617edc6d586239baad65addd848701991e2502eb4"} {"question" "q-4016" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2{e}^{x}-1)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067140/state.json" "file_sha256" "e8f91deb7026399670eb9b3617edc6d586239baad65addd848701991e2502eb4"} {"question" "q-8306" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2yx+y{x}^{2}$ that satisfies $y(1)=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067140/state.json" "file_sha256" "e8f91deb7026399670eb9b3617edc6d586239baad65addd848701991e2502eb4"} {"question" "q-8306" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2yx+y{x}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =y(2x+{x}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2x+{x}^{2} \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (2x+{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =2\\int x\\,\\text{d}x+\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & ={x}^{2}+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the natural logarithm to both sides, we find the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|} & ={e}^{{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}/3+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}/3+C} \\\\ y & =\\pm {e}^{{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}/3+C} \\\\ y & =K{e}^{{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}/3},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K=\\pm {e}^{C}$ is an arbitrary constant. \n\nWe now apply the initial condition $y(1)=1$ to find $K:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(1) & =1 \\\\ K{e}^{{1}^{2}+{1}^{3}/3} & =1 \\\\ K{e}^{4/3} & =1 \\\\ K & ={e}^{-4/3}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2yx+y{x}^{2}$ that satisfies the condition $y(1)=1$ is\n\n$$\ny={e}^{-4/3}\\cdot {e}^{{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}/3}={e}^{({x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}-4)/3}\\,.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067140/state.json" "file_sha256" "e8f91deb7026399670eb9b3617edc6d586239baad65addd848701991e2502eb4"} {"question" "q-8306" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067140/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6c097b443fe834d701881765ef06b2ccca34858447fd15a076ba25dbfa4614f6"} {"question" "q-8306" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067140/state.json" "file_sha256" "e8f91deb7026399670eb9b3617edc6d586239baad65addd848701991e2502eb4"} {"question" "q-8306" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y={e}^{(2{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}-1)/3}"] ["math" "y={e}^{({x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}-4)/3}"] ["math" "y={e}^{({x}^{3}+{x}^{2}-2)/3}"] ["math" "y={e}^{3{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}-1}"] ["math" "y={e}^{{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}-5}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067140/state.json" "file_sha256" "e8f91deb7026399670eb9b3617edc6d586239baad65addd848701991e2502eb4"} {"question" "q-8306" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y={e}^{({x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}-4)/3}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067140/state.json" "file_sha256" "e8f91deb7026399670eb9b3617edc6d586239baad65addd848701991e2502eb4"} {"question" "q-8310" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{y}^{2}}{x}$ that satisfies $y(1)=2.$ Assume that $x>0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067140/state.json" "file_sha256" "e8f91deb7026399670eb9b3617edc6d586239baad65addd848701991e2502eb4"} {"question" "q-8310" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find the particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{y}^{2}}{x} \\\\ \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -\\frac{1}{y} & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C \\\\ \\frac{1}{y} & =-(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C) \\\\ y & =-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAssuming $x>0,$ the general solution is\n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+C},\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nWe now apply the condition $y(1)=2$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(1) & =2 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡1+C} & =2 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{C} & =2 \\\\ C & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the particular solution of $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{y}^{2}}{x}$ that satisfies the condition $y(1)=2$ is\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{-1}{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\frac{1}{2})}=\\frac{2}{1-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}\\,.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067140/state.json" "file_sha256" "e8f91deb7026399670eb9b3617edc6d586239baad65addd848701991e2502eb4"} {"question" "q-8310" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/mu