en initial condition to find the particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}} \\\\ {y}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={x}^{2} \\\\ \\int {y}^{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{3}}{3} & =\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+{C}_{1} \\\\ {y}^{3} & ={x}^{3}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere   $C=3{C}_{1}$ is an arbitrary constant.  \n\nWe now apply the condition $y(1)=2$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{2}^{3} & ={1}^{3}+C \\\\ 8-1 & =C \\\\ C & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we get the particular solution in implicit form:\n\n$$\n{y}^{3}={x}^{3}+7.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067140/state.json" "file_sha256" "e8f91deb7026399670eb9b3617edc6d586239baad65addd848701991e2502eb4"} {"question" "q-14313" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067140/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6c097b443fe834d701881765ef06b2ccca34858447fd15a076ba25dbfa4614f6"} {"question" "q-14313" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067140/state.json" "file_sha256" "e8f91deb7026399670eb9b3617edc6d586239baad65addd848701991e2502eb4"} {"question" "q-14313" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{y}^{3}=2{x}^{3}+2"] ["math" "{y}^{3}=3{x}^{2}+5"] ["math" "{y}^{3}=5{x}^{3}+3"] ["math" "{y}^{3}={x}^{2}+3"] ["math" "{y}^{3}={x}^{3}+7"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067140/state.json" "file_sha256" "e8f91deb7026399670eb9b3617edc6d586239baad65addd848701991e2502eb4"} {"question" "q-14313" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{y}^{3}={x}^{3}+7"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067140/state.json" "file_sha256" "e8f91deb7026399670eb9b3617edc6d586239baad65addd848701991e2502eb4"} {"question" "q-104058" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $(\\frac{1}{xy}-\\frac{1}{x})\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2$ that satisfies $y(1)=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067140/state.json" "file_sha256" "e8f91deb7026399670eb9b3617edc6d586239baad65addd848701991e2502eb4"} {"question" "q-104058" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\frac{1}{xy}-\\frac{1}{x})\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2 \\\\ \\frac{1}{x}(\\frac{1}{y}-1)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2 \\\\ (\\frac{1}{y}-1)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2x \\\\ \\int (\\frac{1}{y}-1)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|-y & ={x}^{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now apply the initial condition $y(1)=1$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1|-1 & ={1}^{2}+C \\\\ 0-1 & =1+C \\\\ C & =-2\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of $(\\frac{1}{xy}-\\frac{1}{x})\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2$ that satisfies the condition $y(1)=1$ in implicit form is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|-y={x}^{2}-2\\,.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067140/state.json" "file_sha256" "e8f91deb7026399670eb9b3617edc6d586239baad65addd848701991e2502eb4"} {"question" "q-104058" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067140/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6c097b443fe834d701881765ef06b2ccca34858447fd15a076ba25dbfa4614f6"} {"question" "q-104058" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067140/state.json" "file_sha256" "e8f91deb7026399670eb9b3617edc6d586239baad65addd848701991e2502eb4"} {"question" "q-104058" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|+y=2{x}^{2}+2"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|+y={x}^{2}+2"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|-y=2{x}^{2}-2"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|-y={x}^{2}-2"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|={x}^{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067140/state.json" "file_sha256" "e8f91deb7026399670eb9b3617edc6d586239baad65addd848701991e2502eb4"} {"question" "q-104058" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|-y={x}^{2}-2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067140/state.json" "file_sha256" "e8f91deb7026399670eb9b3617edc6d586239baad65addd848701991e2502eb4"}] "usage" {"q-8310" [] "q-4016" [] "q-14313" []} "basis" 2236 "retractions" [[17592186101458 :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\frac{dy}{dx} = \\frac{y^{2}}{x}$ that satisfies $y(1) = 2$. Assume that $x > 0$."] [17592186101458 :question/worked-solution "For $x>0$ and the branch through $y(1)=2$, separate and integrate:\n$$\\frac{dy}{y^2}=\\frac{dx}{x},\\qquad -\\frac1y=\\ln x+C.$$\nThe initial condition gives $C=-1/2$, so\n$$y=\\frac2{1-2\\ln x}.$$\nThe maximal interval containing $x=1$ is $0<x<\\sqrt e$."] [17592186101458 :question/difficulty 17592186045465]] "immutable_answers" [17592186100345 17592186100346 17592186100347 17592186100348 17592186100349 17592186296381 17592186296382 17592186296383 17592186296384 17592186296385 17592186335481 17592186335482 17592186335483 17592186335484 17592186335485] "immutable_fields" [[17592186100344 :answer-field/correct] [17592186100344 :answer-field/id] [17592186100344 :answer-field/key] [17592186100344 :answer-field/type] [17592186296380 :answer-field/correct] [17592186296380 :answer-field/id] [17592186296380 :answer-field/key] [17592186296380 :answer-field/type] [17592186335480 :answer-field/correct] [17592186335480 :answer-field/id] [17592186335480 :answer-field/key] [17592186335480 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
